### convention: commit-message-shape
description: Subject line is imperative, under 72 characters, no trailing period.
scope: every commit on every branch
trigger: writing a commit message
status: active
origin: long-standing practice in the plans lineage

A commit subject names the change, not the act of changing. The body carries
the why; the subject carries the what.

### convention: one-commit-per-step
description: Each spec step lands as exactly one commit.
scope: spec-driven coding sessions
trigger: finishing a step
status: active
origin: atomic-step protocol design

One commit per step keeps the step boundary reviewable. A step that needs two
commits is two steps.

### convention: no-dco-on-plans
description: The plans lineage takes no DCO sign-off.
scope: plans and plans-tooling branches
trigger: committing on a plans-lineage branch
status: probation
origin: observed practice, not yet ratified

Code branches contributing upstream require a sign-off. The plans lineage is
internal state and never leaves this repository, so it does not.
